Guidelime.registerGuide([[
[N 42-44 Tanaris]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\From Ratchet by the Barrens road, the Great Lift and the Shimmering Flats to Gadgetzan (flight point, inn): the water survey at Sandsorrow Watch, Gnomish Garbage, the Wastewander bandits, Steamwheedle Port and the Southsea pirates of Lost Rigger Cove, the two WANTED posters, Rhapsody's roc gizzards and the pickups for Feralas and Zul'Farrak.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel 43|r  -  this chapter wants level 43. Every quest here needs 38-42, but the Southsea pirates and Andre Firebeard at Lost Rigger Cove are 44-45, the Wastewander Assassins 44-45 and Caliph Scorpidsting 46. Under 43: do the Rocs, Sandsorrow and the bandit camp first (mobs 40-43), then Waterspring Field, then the Cove; Caliph comes last, at 44 if you can
[OC]|cffffffffTanaris|r  -  you step off the Booty Bay boat in Ratchet with hearth = Booty Bay and bind Gadgetzan on arrival. About 33,600 quest XP on the plain quests and 5g 35s of quest money; every giver, hand-in and mob position comes from the DB, the road in does not
[OC]|cffffcc00Carried in:|r Stoley's Debt (2872) and Tran'rek (2864) from chapter 45 hand in here. Rhapsody's Kalimdor Kocktail (1452) takes its three Roc Gizzards here. From Port to Port (95219) rides on to Feathermoon, and Shipping and Handling (95296) opens Friz's Steamwheedle block below if you have it
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Training:|r no shaman trainer in Tanaris; the level-44 row waits for chapter 48

[OC]|cffffffffThe road to Gadgetzan|r  -  Gadgetzan's flight path is not known yet, so the first trip is by road: Ratchet - the Barrens road - the Great Lift - Thousand Needles - the Shimmering Flats - Tanaris. The DB has no road data: every marker below is unverified. Crossroads, Camp Taurajo and Freewind Post are Horde towns: stay on the road and never stop in their yards. Ghost Wolf for the ride
Ride west from Ratchet to the main road and follow it south past the Crossroads to Camp Taurajo (stay on the road) [G44.5,59.2 The Barrens]
Keep following the road south to the bottom of the Barrens [G46.4,73.9 The Barrens]
Take the Great Lift down into Thousand Needles (the DB has two Great Lift objects, at 29.2,34.2 and 43.3,46.9; the marker is the first, unverified) [G29.2,34.2 Thousand Needles]
Ride east through Thousand Needles to the Mirage Raceway in the Shimmering Flats (Wizzle Brassbolts' spot). |cFFFF0000Danger:|r Freewind Post (Horde) and its level-55 elite wind rider master stand at 45,49 on the way: give it a wide berth [G78.1,77.1 Thousand Needles]

[OC]|cffffffffGadgetzan|r  -  south out of the Shimmering Flats into Tanaris; the town is at 51,28. Every giver stands within 2 units of the inn
At flight master [TAR7823 Bera Stonehammer], get the [P Gadgetzan] flight path [G51.0,29.3 Tanaris]
At [TAR7733 Innkeeper Fizzgrimble], bind your Hearthstone to [S Gadgetzan] (the Booty Bay bind from chapter 45 ends here) [G52.5,27.9 Tanaris]
At [TAR7876 Tran'rek], [QT2864] (390 XP) [QA2865 Scarab Shells] (3,900 XP at the hand-in: 5 Uncracked Scarab Shells from the Scarabs in Zul'Farrak - chapter 51) [G51.6,26.8 Tanaris]
At [TAR7724 Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser], [QA992 Gadgetzan Water Survey] (3,050 XP: use his Untapped Dowsing Widget at the Sandsorrow Watch water hole) [G50.2,27.5 Tanaris]
At the Wanted Poster by the inn, [QA2781 WANTED: Caliph Scorpidsting] (5,050 XP: his head to Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle) [QA2875 WANTED: Andre Firebeard] (3,900 XP: his head to Security Chief Bilgewhizzle in Steamwheedle Port) [G51.8,27.0 Tanaris]
At [TAR14743 Jhordy Lapforge], [QA97536 Gnomish Garbage] (2,900 XP: discard his Crate of Radioactive Refuse 5 times in the desert, a safe distance from Gadgetzan) [G52.3,26.9 Tanaris]
At [TAR7407 Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle], [QA1690 Wastewander Justice] (3,600 XP: 10 Wastewander Bandits and 10 Wastewander Thieves east of town) [G52.5,28.5 Tanaris]
At [TAR7408 Spigot Operator Luglunket] beside him, [QA1707 Water Pouch Bounty] (2,800 XP: 5 Wastewander Water Pouches) [G52.5,28.4 Tanaris]
At the Egg-O-Matic by the inn, [QA2741 The Super Egg-O-Matic] (4,200 XP at the hand-in, requires level 42: a Hippogryph Egg from Feralas, chapter 50; handed in here in chapter 53) [G52.4,27.0 Tanaris]
[O]Only at Cooking 225: at [TAR8125 Dirge Quikcleave], [QA6610 Clamlette Surprise] (3,900 XP at the hand-in: 12 Giant Eggs, 10 Zesty Clam Meat and 20 Alterac Swiss; the Artisan Cooking gate). The DB lists owlbeasts and vultures as the Giant Egg's droppers (the Hinterlands owlbeasts of chapter 48 are on the route); that the Rocs here drop it, as the quest text says, is unverified, and there is no rate in the data; hand-in at Dirge in chapter 53 unless you have it all sooner [G52.6,28.1 Tanaris]

[OC]|cffffffffWest: Rocs and Sandsorrow Watch|r  -  Rocs (41-43, normal) circle south and west of town; the water hole is 13 units west
Kill [TAR5428 Roc] for 3 Roc Gizzards [CI6257,3] (~12% - budget ~25 kills; plain Rocs only, Fire Rocs drop it at ~5%). Nine Rocs sit just south of town, more on the way to Sandsorrow and three east of town on the bandit leg: keep at it until you have three, this is the only gizzard stop before Rhapsody in chapter 48 [G49.5,35.8 Tanaris]
[OC]If an OOX-17/TN Distress Beacon drops (the Rocs and the other Tanaris beasts carry it), keep it for chapter 53
[OC]|cFFFF0000Danger:|r the Sandsorrow Watch water hole (39.0,29.0) stands inside the Sandfury troll camp: Firecallers 43-44, Axe Throwers 43-44 and Hideskinners 42-43, all elite. The nearest stand 0.7-1.5 units east and north-east of the pool; the west side is open (next troll about 3 units away). Come in from the south-west, use the widget at the pool's west edge and leave west
Use the [UI8584 Untapped Dowsing Widget] at the west edge of the Sandsorrow Watch Water Hole (how close you must stand is unverified) [QC992] [G38.6,29.2 Tanaris]
Use the [UI278194 Crate of Radioactive Refuse] 5 times in the open desert between Sandsorrow and Gadgetzan (30 sec cooldown; how far from town counts as "a safe distance" is unverified: move away from the walls if a charge fails) [QC97536] [G44.0,30.0 Tanaris]
At [TAR7724 Senior Surveyor Fizzledowser], [QT992] (3,050 XP + 35s) [G50.2,27.5 Tanaris]
At [TAR14743 Jhordy Lapforge], [QT97536] (2,900 XP) [G52.3,26.9 Tanaris]

[OC]|cffffffffEast: the bandit camp|r  -  Wastewander Thieves 40-41 and Bandits 41-42, normal, x59-66 y23-34; the Rocs at 56-59,25-32 are on the way
Kill 10 [TAR5618 Wastewander Bandit] and 10 [TAR5616 Wastewander Thief] east of Gadgetzan [QC1690] [G62.7,29.3 Tanaris]
Loot Wastewander Water Pouches from the same kills and the next leg's, 5 in all [QC1707] (~33% - budget ~15 kills; the two Wastewander Justice quests kill 44 of these mobs) [G62.7,29.3 Tanaris]
At [TAR7407 Chief Engineer Bilgewhizzle], [QT1690] (3,600 XP + 60s) [QA1691 More Wastewander Justice] (3,750 XP: 10 Shadow Mages, 8 Rogues and 6 Assassins at Waterspring Field) [G52.5,28.5 Tanaris]

[OC]|cffffffffSouth-east: Waterspring Field|r  -  Shadow Mages 41-43, Rogues 43-44, Assassins 44-45, normal, x58-66 y32-41. Finish the pouches here. Caliph Scorpidsting (46, not elite) stands in the middle at 61.8,38.2 among the Rogues and Assassins: leave him for the way home after the Cove
Kill 10 [TAR5617 Wastewander Shadow Mage], 8 [TAR5615 Wastewander Rogue] and 6 [TAR5623 Wastewander Assassin] at Waterspring Field [QC1691] [G61.9,37.4 Tanaris]
Ride north-east to Steamwheedle Port (about 15 units) [G67.1,24.0 Tanaris]

[OC]|cffffffffSteamwheedle Port|r  -  the goblin port on the north-east coast; every giver stands within 2 units of 67,23.5
At [TAR7881 Stoley], [QT2872] (390 XP) [QA2873 Stoley's Shipment] (3,900 XP: Stoley's Shipment from the Stolen Cargo at Lost Rigger Cove) [G67.1,24.0 Tanaris]
At [TAR7882 Security Chief Bilgewhizzle], [QA8366 Southsea Shakedown] (3,900 XP: 10 each of Southsea Pirates, Freebooters, Dock Workers and Swashbucklers) [G67.1,23.9 Tanaris]
At [TAR8579 Yeh'kinya], [QA3520 Screecher Spirits] (3,750 XP at the hand-in: capture 3 screecher spirits in Feralas with Yeh'kinya's Bramble - chapter 47; handed in here in chapter 51) [G67.0,22.4 Tanaris]
[O]Only if you carry Shipping and Handling (95296): at [TAR260405 Wharfmaster Steamfizzle], [QT95296] (315 XP) [QA95383 Shipping and Handling] (315 XP: Friz's Secret Stash to Tazzik) [G67.6,23.1 Tanaris]
[O]Only if you took 95383: at [TAR260857 Tazzik], [QT95383] (315 XP) [QA95312 Coming to Collect] (315 XP: speak with Fizbuz Mithril in Gadgetzan) [G67.3,24.0 Tanaris]

[OC]|cffffffffLost Rigger Cove|r  -  south down the coast (about 23 units) to the Southsea pirates, all 44-45 and normal, x71-76 y42-49. |cFFFF0000Danger:|r Kregg Keelhaul (47, rare) stands at 73.2,48.7, 1.6 units from Andre Firebeard, and Southsea Kidnappers (45) stand among them
Kill 10 each of [TAR7855 Southsea Pirate], [TAR7856 Southsea Freebooter], [TAR7857 Southsea Dock Worker] and [TAR7858 Southsea Swashbuckler] in the cove [QC8366] [G73.3,46.3 Tanaris]
Loot Stoley's Shipment from the Stolen Cargo (five spawn points, all at 72.1-72.2,46.7-46.8) [QC2873] [G72.2,46.8 Tanaris]
Kill [TAR7883 Andre Firebeard] (45, not elite) for Firebeard's Head [QC2875] (~59% - one kill only, then abandon) [G73.4,47.1 Tanaris]
[O]No head from Andre: abandon WANTED: Andre Firebeard [QS2875] [G73.4,47.1 Tanaris]
[OC]|cffffcc00Ship Schedules:|r the four Southsea types drop a Pirate's Footlocker now and then; open every one. About one in seven holds a Ship Schedule, about 0.76% per kill in all: never farm it
[O]Only if a Ship Schedule turned up: use it to start [QA2876 Ship Schedules] (4,850 XP: report it to Security Chief Bilgewhizzle) [G73.3,46.3 Tanaris]

[OC]|cffffffffBack to Steamwheedle Port|r
At [TAR7881 Stoley], [QT2873] (3,900 XP + 50s) [QA2874 Deliver to MacKinley] (3,900 XP at the hand-in: Stoley's Bottle to "Sea Wolf" MacKinley in Booty Bay - chapter 49) [G67.1,24.0 Tanaris]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (8366, choice):|r take |cff66ff66Southsea Mojo Boots|r (cloth feet +11 Int +8 spell damage, 29.1 on the weights) and wear them in place of the Verger Greaves (30.0, a tie); the Southsea Head Bucket is plate: pass. Sell the Greaves (44s 28c)
At [TAR7882 Security Chief Bilgewhizzle], [QT8366] (3,900 XP + 65s) [QT2875] (3,900 XP + 1g 30s) [G67.1,23.9 Tanaris]
[O]Only with the Ship Schedule: at [TAR7882 Security Chief Bilgewhizzle], [QT2876] (4,850 XP + 1g 30s) [G67.1,23.9 Tanaris]

